title: Volume Shadow Copy Deletion via PowerShell WMI
status: experimental
description: Detects PowerShell removing Volume Shadow Copies through the Win32_Shadowcopy WMI class, which ransomware uses to prevent recovery. Observed right after each Akira locker.exe execution.
references:
    - https://thedfirreport.com/2026/06/29/from-bing-search-to-ransomware-bumblebee-and-adaptixc2-deliver-akira-3/
author: Sümeyra Yüksel
date: 2026/10/20
tags:
    - attack.impact
    - attack.t1490
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_img:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\powershell.exe'
            - '\pwsh.exe'
    selection_class:
        CommandLine|contains: 'Win32_Shadowcopy'
    selection_remove:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'Remove-WmiObject'
            - 'Remove-CimInstance'
            - '.Delete()'
    condition: all of selection_*
fields:
    - Image
    - ParentImage
    - CommandLine
    - User
falsepositives:
    - Backup or storage maintenance scripts that clean up shadow copies
level: high
